bbq-predictor (0.1.0-5) unstable; urgency=low

  * The publisher fetches each band at its own interval, remembered across
    rounds, and completes the head from the last one: about half the
    Weather Underground requests per station.
  * Messages that named a cause nothing had tested now say what happened.
  * Build-Depends names Qt's SQLite driver for the tests, and the server
    half builds alone for Devuan daedalus (make deb-daedalus).

 -- Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:24:12 +0200

bbq-predictor (0.1.0-4) unstable; urgency=low

  * Ask a different Weather Underground page on each of the three attempts
    for the key, since what each page serves changes within minutes.

 -- Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:02:19 +0200

bbq-predictor (0.1.0-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * bbq-predictor-serve records the stations clients ask for, with
    --demand, and bbq-predictor-publish fetches them: up to 50 beside the
    configured one, dropped after 14 days unasked, within 2000 Weather
    Underground requests an hour. The applet asks again about a station
    the server does not publish, hourly, so it notices one being added.

 -- Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:20:32 +0200

bbq-predictor (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Publish from bbq-predictor-publish, built on QtCore, QtNetwork and
    QtSql alone, so a server needs no display and no desktop libraries.
    The applet refuses --publish and the signing-key options by name.
  * Move the five-minute round -- the timer, the cron line, its
    configuration and the bbq-predictor account -- to bbq-predictor-server,
    and run the publisher from it.

 -- Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:03:09 +0200

bbq-predictor (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First package.  Installs the applet and a systemd timer that fetches
    the bands on its own clock, so the archive advances and verification
    accumulates without the window being open.

 -- Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 13:20:14 +0200
